Toy antenna-array rehearsal
===========================

This experiment rehearses the complete nested-interface construction on
smooth closed PEC surfaces. One station consists of four small ellipsoids
(the toy leaves) above one oblate ellipsoid (the toy dish). Four translated
copies form a 2-by-2 array. It tests symmetry reuse, compression, feedback,
and reuse of a precomputed station response; it does not model paraboloid
focusing, feed ports, material losses, or the ground's electromagnetic response.

Run from the repository root after building the usual project dependencies:

  run('startup.m')
  result = test_toy_array_scattering(8,28,1e-5,true);

The arguments are physical patch order, proxy polar order, joint-ID
tolerance, and whether to run the four-station array stage. The proxy has
nproxy polar nodes and 2*nproxy azimuthal nodes. Both interfaces use this
order. The main function defaults to (8,28,1e-5,true).

A cheaper plumbing check is:

  test_toy_array_scattering(4,16,1e-4,false);

That coarse run is expected to be inaccurate and can fail the final accuracy
assertion. It still saves its errors and interfaces under test/results before
asserting. A small ID tolerance does not compensate for coarse physical or
proxy quadrature. The refined command above is a run configuration, not a
claim that physical mesh convergence has been established.

Geometry and conventions
------------------------

toy_antenna_array_geometry(norder) returns model and physical. The latter
contains body, leaves{1:4}, feed, and station surfers for ONE station. The
leaves are in counterclockwise order, each built by rotating the same base
mesh and its tangent frame. physical.feed merges these four surfaces;
physical.station merges the body first and the feed second.

Lengths are in wavelengths, lambda=1, k=2*pi. The body's horizontal diameter
is 1, and its bottom is 1/6 above z=0. Scaling the diameter to 6 m therefore
gives the provisional 1 m clearance from the HIRAX email correspondence.
This preserves the geometric height/diameter ratio, not the real array's
electrical size at its operating frequencies. The inner sphere surrounds
only the leaves. The outer oblate ellipsoid encloses the whole station and
the inner sphere. The outer proxies are disjoint and remain above z=0.
The plane z=0 is only a location reference in this free-space experiment.

The fields use exp(-i*omega*t), epsilon=mu=1. Physical NRCCIE unknowns are
interleaved [ju,jv,rho] per physical node. Proxy data are interleaved
d=[Eu,Ev,Hu,Hv] per proxy node, in outward-oriented orthonormal tangent
frames. These trace values do not include quadrature weights.

The symbols below have the following meanings:

  K(S -> T): evaluate E and H on targets T from NRCCIE density on S.
  Q(P -> T): outward Stratton-Chu evaluation from proxy trace on P to T.
  L_P:       extract the four tangential components on P from E and H.
  R_S:       form the NRCCIE incident-field right-hand side on S.

Q includes source quadrature weights. It reproduces an outgoing field
outside P. For an incident field regular throughout the interior of P,
-Q reproduces that incident field inside P. Neither use requires solving
a first-kind equivalent-source equation. No on-surface jump evaluation is
used in these proxy-to-body or inter-proxy maps.

1. Reuse C4 quadrature and solve the four-leaf system
-------------------------------------------------

  [A_f,info,cache] = toy_fourfold_system(leaves,opts,eps_quad,run_reference);
  q_f = cache.solve(rhs);

opts contains zk, alpha, and jump, with optional batch_size. Only one target
block row of quadrature corrections is computed: one self block and three
relative interleaf blocks. Rotation gives the other rows, so construction
uses 4 correction blocks instead of 16. Cartesian gradient corrections are
rotated as vectors. The existing fourfold_quad_corr_mats and
fourfold_apply_quad_corr routines perform this reuse. The helper converts
their clockwise indexing convention to the toy geometry's original order.

Tangent-basis NRCCIE density components do not need an extra Cartesian
rotation when their tangent frames rotate with the geometry. The helper
checks this covariance and constructs only four corrected system blocks
B_0,...,B_3. With leaf indices 0,...,3, the complete system satisfies

  (A_f)_{ij} = B_{(j-i) mod 4}.

It is block circulant. The four Fourier-mode matrices are

  D_m = sum_{r=0}^3 exp(2*pi*i*m*r/4)*B_r,  m=0,...,3.

cache.solve applies fft across the leaf index, solves with four smaller
LU factors D_m, and applies ifft. This handles arbitrary incident fields
and arbitrary densities; it does not require a symmetric right-hand side.
The helper retains the dense A_f for residual checks in this toy experiment,
but does not factor the full four-leaf matrix.

cache.corrections can be passed directly to fourfold_apply_quad_corr in the
original leaf ordering. Setting run_reference=true independently builds
the complete merged-feed quadrature and compares all sixteen blocks and
the compact correction apply. The main pipeline instead obtains this
independent comparison from its full five-body station reference, avoiding
a duplicate feed-reference computation.

2. Construct the square feed scattering matrix on the inner sphere
----------------------------------------------------------------

For the feed geometry S_f and its enclosing sphere P_f, define

  B_f = -R_f*Q(P_f -> S_f),
  C_f = L_f*K(S_f -> P_f).

B_f maps regular incoming proxy traces to the physical BIE right-hand side.
C_f maps solved physical densities to outgoing proxy traces. The function
maxwell_build_interface(P,mapfun,A,tol,leaf_points,label,solvefun) requests
blocks of these maps as needed. Here solvefun is the C4 cache.solve above.

A deterministic multilevel row ID of the normalized joint map

  [B_f'/norm(B_f,'fro'), C_f/norm(C_f,'fro')]

selects whole proxy points, retaining all four trace components per point.
It first compresses spatial subgroups, then combines and recompresses their
skeletons. There is no randomized sketch. A single interpolation U_f gives

  B_f approximately B_fI*U_f',
  C_f approximately U_f*C_fI,
  S_f = C_fI*(A_f inverse applied to B_fI).

I denotes the four-component DOFs of the selected points. The scattering
matrix S_f is square, of size 4*number_of_skeleton_points. The full proxy
matrix C_f*(A_f inverse applied to B_f) is never formed. The returned fields
are Scat, nodes, proxy, input_projection=U_f', and output_interpolation=U_f.

For a new incident trace din_f,

  a_f = U_f'*din_f,
  b_f = S_f*a_f,
  dout_f approximately U_f*b_f.

a_f is a projection of the full incident trace, not incident samples at
the selected points. b_f represents the outgoing trace at the skeleton
points. Shared points make S_f square without identifying incoming and
outgoing fields or imposing symmetry on them.

3. Couple the compressed feed to the physical toy dish
----------------------------------------------------

Let A_d be the corrected body NRCCIE matrix and q_d its physical density.
The coupling maps are

  G_fd = U_f'*L_f*K(S_d -> P_f),
  G_df = R_d*Q(P_f -> S_d)*U_f.

The body is outside the feed sphere, so its outgoing exterior evaluation
is valid on the body. The hybrid system is

  H = [ A_d,         -G_df;
        -S_f*G_fd,    identity ],

  H*[q_d;b_f] = [ R_d*EHinc_d;
                  S_f*U_f'*din_f ].

Solving H includes repeated feedback between the body and all four leaves.
This construction accesses the feed through P_f, U_f, and S_f. The small
physical density is recovered later only for diagnostic comparisons.

4. Construct one whole-station interface on the outer ellipsoid
-------------------------------------------------------------

For outer proxy P_o, the incoming and outgoing maps of the hybrid system are

  B_o = [ -R_d*Q(P_o -> S_d);
          -S_f*U_f'*L_f*Q(P_o -> P_f) ],

  C_o = [ L_o*K(S_d -> P_o), L_o*Q(P_f -> P_o)*U_f ].

The minus signs in B_o reconstruct the incident field inside P_o. Apply
the same joint point-ID construction to B_o and C_o, then form only

  S_o = C_oI*(H inverse applied to B_oI).

This square S_o includes all feed/body feedback. maxwell_ellipsoid supplies
the correct ellipsoid normals, tangent frames, and surface weights. The
outer surface need not be a sphere. Both interfaces retain explicit U for
this small demonstration; weak compression can still produce large
candidate blocks. Physical matrices and H are also dense here.

5. Reuse the station matrix and couple the four-station array
----------------------------------------------------------

toy_array_coupling translates the same proxy and skeletons by the four
model.station_shifts. The pipeline constructs S_o once, and this helper
reuses that same matrix for the other three stations. No independent scattering-matrix construction
is performed for those translated copies. The stations have identical
orientations; translation leaves their local tangent frames unchanged.

With U=U_o, S=S_o, define the inter-station translation and incident maps

  T_ij = U'*L_i*Q(P_j -> P_i)*U,  i != j,
  a_i = U'*din_i.

The coupled compressed array equations are

  b_i - S*sum_{j != i} T_ij*b_j = S*a_i.

GMRES solves this compressed system with its identity diagonal and a
1e-12 relative tolerance. The compressed matrix is explicit in this toy
implementation, but it is not factored as one large dense LU.

These equations include repeated scattering among all four stations. The twelve
directed interactions have eight distinct translation offsets on this
square grid; each offset map is constructed once. Target batches avoid
forming the full proxy-to-proxy field matrices. For separated targets
outside all outer proxies, the scattered field is

  EHsc(targets) = sum_i Q(P_i -> targets)*U*b_i.

The target field contains both E and H. Add EHinc at the targets for the
total field. The current quantities are fields and scattering responses,
not receiving voltages or port S-parameters.

Independent validation and saved output
--------------------------------------

The station check solves the independently assembled full five-body
corrected NRCCIE. It checks C4 quadrature reuse, physical and hybrid solve
residuals, incident reconstruction, proxy traces, and exterior E/H fields
for new plane waves and exterior electric and magnetic dipoles. Separate
Green-representation and B/C-ID errors distinguish proxy quadrature from
compression error. A control omits feed/body feedback.

For the array, the reference is the TRUE full corrected NRCCIE, including
its charge-continuity cross terms. nrccie_apply applies it with the FMM;
GMRES uses the full single-station NRCCIE matrix as a block preconditioner.
Translated station corrections are reused, and independent inter-station
near corrections are constructed. This avoids a dense full-array physical
matrix. It does not substitute the field-only cross expression -R*K for
the actual NRCCIE blocks. The actual unpreconditioned residual is checked.
Another control evaluates the four stations without array feedback.

The reported construction savings (4 rather than 16 feed correction
blocks; one station scattering matrix plus three reuses) describe the
production construction. They exclude extra independent reference and
validation computations. The full validation run intentionally does more
work than would be needed to apply the precomputed interfaces alone.

The main function saves a station checkpoint before array work and saves
the complete result before its final pass assertion. Files are named

  test/results/toy_array_p<norder>_q<nproxy>_<tol-tag>.mat

For example, the refined command above writes

  test/results/toy_array_p8_q28_1em05.mat.

Useful saved fields include model, feed, outer, symmetry, stats, errors,
timings, fields, targets, and array. The default acceptance threshold for
the station/array exterior-field comparison is 5e-3 relative to the same
physical discretization. The independent reference does not prove physical
mesh convergence: increasing physical patch order and proxy order is still
required for a continuum-accuracy study. The plotted ground clearance is
retained throughout, but ground reflection is not part of these equations.

Measured rehearsal (physical order 8, proxy order 28, ID tolerance 1e-5)
---------------------------------------------------------------------

  Four-leaf physical unknowns                        5832
  Fourier-mode factor sizes                   4 x (1458 by 1458)
  Feed proxy points / retained skeleton points       1568 / 485
  Feed scattering matrix                            1940 by 1940
  Full station / hybrid unknowns                     7290 / 3398
  Outer proxy points / retained skeleton points      1568 / 718
  Station scattering matrix                         2872 by 2872
  Array physical / compressed unknowns              29160 / 11488
  Station matrix builds / translated reuses          1 / 3

Maximum relative errors over ten station test fields (eight plane waves
and two dipoles), or four array test fields (two directions, two polarizations):

  C4 matrix vs independently corrected matrix        5.43e-12
  C4 correction application                         3.03e-12
  Feed B / C compression                        3.18e-6 / 3.12e-6
  Outer B / C compression                       2.06e-6 / 2.89e-6
  Feed-interface exterior field                     1.08e-3
  Hybrid feed/body exterior field                   3.51e-4
  Outer-interface exterior field                    3.94e-3
  Outer Green reconstruction of full reference       3.91e-3
  Feed/body feedback omitted                        6.10e-2
  Coupled four-station exterior field                4.49e-3
  Inter-station coupling omitted                    2.96e-1
  Full-array true NRCCIE residual                   1.23e-9

The compressed array GMRES took 12 iterations for each of four right-hand
sides; the independent physical reference took 9--10 iterations. One local
four-thread run took 857.4 seconds, including all independent validation.
The feed and outer interface stages took 286.2 and 367.2 seconds; array
construction, solve, and validation took 169.8 seconds. These are measured
prototype times, not scaling estimates or predicted symmetry speedups.

The additional physics-only check is reproducible without constructing S:

  refinement = check_toy_physics([8,10],[28,40]);

For its two polarizations, increasing physical order from 8 to 10 changed
the direct field by at most 1.79e-3 and reduced the Green reconstruction
error from 1.48e-3 to 2.90e-4. Changing proxy order from 28 to 40 had little
effect. This identifies physical discretization as the dominant error in
this run; the 1e-5 ID tolerance is not the total field accuracy.
The refinement data are saved in test/results/toy_physics_refinement.mat.

To inspect the complete saved result without loading native BIE libraries:

  r = load('test/results/toy_array_p8_q28_1em05.mat');
  plot_toy_array_scattering(r,'on');

This writes the sibling _summary.png and _summary.fig. The native solver
run saved data and printed TOY_ARRAY_SCATTERING_PASS before the existing
MATLAB native-library shutdown crash. A separate pure MATLAB process
reloaded both interfaces, checked skeleton identities and ellipsoid
orientation/volume, reapplied the saved array coefficients, and compared
the dense station reference with the independent FMM reference (9.45e-12
relative difference). That verification passed and exited normally.
